  "adjudication_note": "The tail of the heading measurement after batches 25-30, read rather than assumed. Before mining it the instrument was corrected: a heading contrasting two subjects (`Top-Down & Bottom-Up`, `Time-Weighted x Money Weighted Rate of Return`) names two concepts and not a third, and scoring it `partial` while both are registered would have sent batches chasing an artifact of the metric — the exact failure of the OOV target this instrument replaces. The correction moved coverage 1.4 points, so the metric was not materially inflated; checking cost one run and the answer could have gone either way. What remains here is real: `divulgação de informações` 16 occurrences, `risco total` 15, `estilos` 15, `gestão de carteiras de renda fixa` 13, `risco de reinvestimento` 11. Also `value-at-risk` hyphenated, 16 occurrences against 1 for the spaced spelling that was the only one registered.",
